  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK Aid Transparency review</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A programme of work to be undertaken by Publish What You Fund to monitor and help improve the transparency of aid across HMG. The bulk of the work will be in the form of a tailored review, rather than the construction of a ranking as took place in 2020. This review will require substantial engagement with the other government departments (OGDs) currently spending ODA. A methodology for the review, including the quantity and quality of IATI data currently being published, will be developed and final report outputs will be determined. 
Publish What You Fund will undertake an assessment of the following UK aid spending departments (those listed represent all government departments with an annual ODA budget in excess of &#xA3;100mn according to the 2023 Statistics on International Development):

&#x2022;	Home Office 
&#x2022;	Department of Health and Social Care (DHSC)
&#x2022;	Ministry of Housing, Communities and Local Government (MHCLG)
&#x2022;	Department for Energy Security and Net Zero (DESNZ)
&#x2022;	Department for Work and Pensions (DWP)
&#x2022;	Department for Education (DfE)
&#x2022;	Department for Science, Innovation and Technology (DSIT)
&#x2022;	Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs (DEFRA)</narrative>
  </description>
